WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
A leaf sits in sunlight.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.780
Carbon dioxide comes in from the air.

3
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.940
Water comes up from the roots.

4
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.350
Out of the leaf comes oxygen.

5
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.540
Long ago, tiny cells doing the same job
gave Earth an atmosphere with oxygen in

6
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.400
it.

7
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.250
Both inputs contain oxygen atoms.

8
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.670
So which one did the
released oxygen come from?

9
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.720
In this mission, you'll follow
every atom through photosynthesis,

10
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.880
from the two inputs to sugar and oxygen.

11
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.720
Then you'll read the data
from a real experiment,

12
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:36.840
from 1941, that tagged oxygen
atoms with a heavy isotope.

13
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: find out which of the
two inputs the oxygen came from.
